concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-25 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "25 Section 25"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-25 ;
    values:originalText "(1) Where a person sentenced to a term of imprisonment in respect of a federal offence has had a licence granted under the Principal Act in respect of that sentence revoked under paragraph 19a (5) (b) of the Principal Act before the commencing day, then, whether or not the person has been arrested and brought before a prescribed authority before that day, the Principal Act continues to apply in relation to that person and that sentence, on and after that day, until that sentence is fully served, as if the amendments made by Division 1 of this Part had not been made.  Crimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2) No. 4, 1990 (2) Where a person sentenced to a term of imprisonment in respect of a federal offence has had a licence granted under the Principal Act cancelled by a prescribed authority under subsection 19a (7) of the Principal Act before the commencing day, the Principal Act continues to apply in relation to that person and that sentence, on and after that day, until that sentence is fully served, as if the amendments made by Division 1 of this Part had not been made. Sentences and orders under subsection 19b (1), 20 (1) or 20ab (1) of the Principal Act" ;
    skos:definition "(1) Where a person sentenced to a term of imprisonment in respect of a federal offence has had a licence granted under the Principal Act in respect of that sentence revoked under paragraph 19a (5) (b) of the Principal Act before the commencing day, then, whether or not the person has been arrested and brought before a prescribed authority before that day, the Principal Act continues to apply in relation to that person and that sentence, on and after that day, until that sentence is fully served, as if the amendments made by Division 1 of this Part had not been made.  Crimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2) No. 4, 1990 (2) Where a person sentenced to a term of imprisonment in respect of a federal offence has had a licence granted under the Principal Act cancelled by a prescribed authority under subsection 19a (7) of the Principal Act before the commencing day, the Principal Act continues to apply in relation to that person and that sentence, on and after that day, until that sentence is fully served, as if the amendments made by Division 1 of this Part had not been made. Sentences and orders under subsection 19b (1), 20 (1) or 20ab (1) of the Principal Act"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6d4857e503e0d1a7f4531f47d1b46514a8fd121bee0dd22368b12d6b348cf335" ;
    cof:pageNumber "59"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Continues to apply in relation to a person and sentence after revocation or cancellation of licence." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-legislation-amendment-act.pdf> ;
    dc:source "crimes-legislation-amendment-act.pdf, p.59" ;
    cml:asserts concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-25-norm .
