doc:sec-32 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "32 Section 32" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) Where a person sentenced to a term of imprisonment in respect of a federal offence has had a parole order made under the Commonwealth Prisoners Act 1967 in respect of that sentence revoked under paragraph 5 (5) (b) of that Act, or by operation of subsection 5 (7) of that Act, before the commencing day, then, whether or not the person has been arrested and brought before a prescribed authority before that day, that Act continues to apply in relation to that person and that sentence on and after that day, until that sentence is fully served, as if that Act had not been repealed and the amendments made by Division 1 of this Part had not been made.  Crimes Legislation Amendment (No. 2) No. 4, 1990 (2) Where a person sentenced to a term of imprisonment in respect of a federal offence has had a parole order made under the Commonwealth Prisoners Act 1967 in respect of that sentence cancelled by a prescribed authority under section 6 of that Act before the commencing day, that Act continues to apply in relation to that person and that sentence, on and after the commencing day, until that sentence is fully served, as if that Act had not been repealed and the amendments made by Division 1 of this Part had not been made. Application of State or Territory remission or reduction laws to certain federal non-parole periods" ;
    cof:pageNumber "63"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-sec-33 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "33 Section 33"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-33 ;
    values:originalText "Nothing in this Part shall be taken to affect the application of a law of a State or Territory providing for the remission or reduction of State or Territory non-parole periods of imprisonment to federal non-parole periods of imprisonment fixed in respect of federal sentences of imprisonment imposed before the commencing day. Further consequential amendments" ;
    skos:definition "Nothing in this Part shall be taken to affect the application of a law of a State or Territory providing for the remission or reduction of State or Territory non-parole periods of imprisonment to federal non-parole periods of imprisonment fixed in respect of federal sentences of imprisonment imposed before the commencing day. Further consequential amendments"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8680a83fbd654c2ce9c7187ba5e44f7c332e980ba2a3a288a7c9550731129721" ;
    cof:pageNumber "64"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "No effect on State/Territory laws regarding remission of non-parole periods." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
